# WS1-08. Source: spec/13-data-inclusion.md §1 ("A module-level initializer is
# also a constant context (E10213), so an embedded asset can back a module-level
# let") and §2 ("bound with a module-level let, it stays writable"). File "abcd":
# after PAL[0] = 'z' the bytes are 122, 98. Note: spec/04-expressions.md §16
# says a module-level let initializer is runtime and not a constant context.
expect: output
contrast: PAL[0] = 'z'; ==> PAL[0] = 'y';
contrast-expect: output
--- output
122 98 4
--- contrast-output
121 98 4
